# XSH wcsxfrm() and wcsxfrm_l()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests run in the POSIX locale (selected with setlocale(LC_ALL, "C")).
# Only values the text defines are checked: the length returned, the order
# relation between the transformed strings and the collation function, and
# that no more than n codes are written. The locale-object test uses a
# locale made with newlocale() for "C"; a failure to make one is UNRESOLVED.
# Destinations are filled with L'X' first, so that codes written past n show.

assertion  XSH.wcsxfrm.001
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With room for the whole result, wcsxfrm() of "abc" returns a
           length equal to the wcslen() of the string it stored, and a null
           code ends the result at that index.
test       t/001-length.c

assertion  XSH.wcsxfrm.002
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       For every pair taken from twelve strings of portable characters,
           the sign of wcscmp() on the two transformed strings equals the
           sign of wcscoll() on the originals.
test       t/002-order.c

assertion  XSH.wcsxfrm.003
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With n 3 on "abcdef", no code at index 3 or later is written, and
           the value returned equals the one returned when there is room for
           everything.
test       t/003-n-bound.c

assertion  XSH.wcsxfrm.004
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With n 0 the destination may be a null pointer: the call returns
           the same length as the call with room for everything.
test       t/004-n-zero.c

assertion  XSH.wcsxfrm.005
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       wcsxfrm_l() with a locale object for "C" gives, for pairs of
           strings, transformed strings whose wcscmp() sign equals that of
           wcscoll_l() on the originals.
test       t/005-locale-object.c

assertion  XSH.wcsxfrm.006
anchor     functions/wcsxfrm.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       wcsxfrm() and wcsxfrm_l() leave errno unchanged when they
           succeed, both when it is 0 and when it is EDOM.
test       t/006-errno-kept.c
